# `databricks bundle` writes per-target deployment state and sync snapshots here. It is local
# machine state, and `.databricks/sync-snapshots/` in particular changes on every sync.
.databricks/

# Python / uv workspace
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# uv.lock is deliberately NOT committed.
#
# `uv lock` resolves against whatever package index the developer has configured, and bakes
# those artifact URLs into the file -- so a lockfile committed from a machine pointed at an
# internal mirror publishes that hostname and breaks CI for everyone outside that network.
# It happened. Until there is a single agreed index that every contributor and CI resolve
# through, the lockfile is a local artifact.
#
# NOTE: this pattern has no leading slash, so it matches at ANY depth. That deliberately covers
# `packages/shellbox-app/src/uv.lock`, the DEPLOY root's lockfile, which `make app-lock`
# regenerates on every deploy for the reason above plus one more -- it is rewritten to public
# package hosts after it is generated, so the committed and the local copy could never agree.
uv.lock

# The pre-rewrite copy `make app-lock`'s `sed -i.bak` leaves behind. That target removes it once
# both lock checks pass, so a file here means a check failed and the bytes are kept for reading.
uv.lock.bak
